                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1000">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1000"/>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>The Boinville family had a long association with the Godwins. Cornelia was the daughter of <persName key="BOI02">Chastel</persName> and 
      <persName key="BOI01">Harriet</persName> and the family became close to the Godwins in the 
      1800s. Cornelia married <persName key="TUR01">Thomas Turner</persName>, another longtime advocate of Godwin, in 1812. 
      In the spring of 1814, before <persName key="SHE01">Percy Shelley</persName> and Mary Wollstonecraft Godwin became close, Shelley, 
      according to his wife Harriet, had been very attentive to Cornelia in her husband's absence. Godwin told Turner, who took his wife to 
Devon, ensuring she did not see Shelley again. (St Clair, p. 360)</p>
                        <p>For a fuller discussion see <persName key="BOI01">Harriet Boinville</persName></p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">St Clair</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
